WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.230
1798.

2
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:05.690
Thomas Malthus argues that
population, unchecked,

3
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:11.810
grows in a geometrical ratio;
food, only in an arithmetical one.

4
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.970
Population outruns food, until checks act:

5
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:19.310
fewer births, or more deaths
from hunger and disease.

6
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.460
Since 1961, world population
has grown about 2.6 times:

7
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:29.930
3.06 billion to 8.06 billion in 2023.

8
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.610
Has food per person risen or fallen?

9
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.170
Fallen sharply, as Malthus predicted?

10
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.190
Or can it not be measured?

11
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.690
In this mission, you'll set
Malthus against Ester Boserup,

12
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.330
who argued the reverse,
and test both with data.

13
00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.110
Then you'll judge the UN's
Sustainable Development Goals,

14
00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.650
using the 2026 progress report.

15
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.430
Your mission: find out whether food
per person has risen or fallen,

16
00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.530
and what that means for Malthus.
